=> Question 2 - Maintain Unique Transaction IDs

     -> Continue in the SAME PROGRAM.

     -> Now the bank wants another collection that stores
        transaction IDs only once.

     -> Use the following transaction IDs:

          TXN103
          TXN101
          TXN105
          TXN103
          TXN102
          TXN101
          TXN104

     -> Requirements:

          -> Duplicate transaction IDs must not be stored.

          -> The order in which a transaction ID first appeared
             must be maintained.

          -> Display the first transaction ID.

          -> Display the last transaction ID.

          -> Move:
               TXN105
             to the beginning.

          -> Move:
               TXN103
             to the end.

          -> Display all unique transaction IDs
             from last to first.

          -> Remove the transaction ID currently
             appearing first.

     -> Do not use indexes.

     -> Decide:

          -> Which interface should be used?

          -> Which implementation should be used?

          -> Which methods are suitable?



