=> Question 5 - Transaction Priority Update

     -> Continue using the transaction/status map
        created in Question 4.

     -> Assume the map currently contains:

          TXN101 -> "FAILED"
          TXN105 -> "PENDING"
          TXN102 -> "SUCCESS"
          TXN104 -> "FAILED"

     -> Perform the following business operations:

          -> TXN102 becomes the highest-priority transaction.

          -> Move TXN102 to the beginning.

          -> At the same time, update its value from:

               "SUCCESS"

             to:

               "RETRY_SUCCESS"

          -> TXN101 later becomes the lowest-priority transaction.

          -> Move TXN101 to the end.

          -> Update its value from:

               "FAILED"

             to:

               "RETRY_PENDING"

     -> Important:

          -> The same transaction ID must NOT appear twice.

     -> After the updates:

          -> Display the complete map.

          -> Display the first entry.

          -> Display the last entry.

          -> Display the map in reverse order.

     -> Pay attention to what happens when the key
        already exists.

     -> Decide the appropriate methods.



