=> Question 7 - Transaction Map Views

     -> Continue using a sequenced transaction/status map.

     -> Use the following data:

          TXN101 -> "SUCCESS"
          TXN102 -> "FAILED"
          TXN103 -> "SUCCESS"
          TXN104 -> "CLOSED"
          TXN105 -> "SUCCESS"

     -> Obtain three separate views:

          -> All transaction IDs.

          -> All transaction statuses.

          -> All complete transaction/status entries.

     -> The encounter order of the original map
        must be preserved in all three views.

     -> For each view:

          -> Display the first element.

          -> Display the last element.

          -> Display the elements in reverse encounter order.

     -> Then understand through your program:

          -> Why can "SUCCESS" appear multiple times?

          -> Why can TXN101 not appear multiple times
             as separate keys?

          -> Why does the key view behave like a set?

          -> Why does the entry view behave like a set?

          -> Why does the value view NOT behave like a set?

     -> Decide the appropriate Java 21 methods.



